  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1005 AM MDT Tue Jun 30 2026\n\nContinuing from yesterday, breezy southwest winds out west by\nvirtue of a trough over Arizona, Nevada, and California meets a \nridge over Tennessee, Kentucky, and Arkansas, funneling a plume of\nmoisture from Chihuauha into Hudspeth County for today. An \nisolated (20-30%) chance of storms may occur in eastern El Paso \nCounty as well, and any outflows generated from these storms could\ngenerate blowing dust this afternoon and evening. Possible\nisolated showers may occur in western New Mexico, though chances\nof storms happening there are slim (10-20%). Temperatures will\nbottom out at the mid-90s for the region today, and starting\ntomorrow, a gradual warm up will occur.\n\nDry air will push into New Mexico as we enter July. By Friday, the\nmoisture plume will evaporate and an upper- high will make its \npresence known over the Four Corners. Storm chances as we approach\nthe holiday weekend will be limited mainly to the mountains. Hot \nand dry conditions will be in place for most of the CWA for the \nFourth of July weekend.",
